# The hags' kitchen garden on the hill (prop bonegrinder_hag_garden): belladonna, mandrake, poppies. Speak with Plants
# (2024 PHB; docs/story/talking_creatures.md): plants tell what passed them in the last day. Last night Bella flew home
# low over them and hid her broom in the loft's rafters (rafters_broom).

~ garden
narrate examine:bonegrinder_hag_garden
* [if spell:speak_with_plants and not flag.hag_garden_spoke and not flag.bella_slain and not flag.bella_fled and not flag.bonegrinder_burned] Ask the garden what went by last night. -> speaks
* [if not spell:speak_with_plants and not flag.hag_garden_spoke and not flag.bella_slain and not flag.bella_fled and not flag.bonegrinder_burned] [knows:speak_with_plants] (Cast Speak with Plants, and ask the garden what went by last night.) -> cast
* [if spell:speak_with_plants or knows:speak_with_plants] Leave the garden alone. -> END
-> END

~ cast
cast speak_with_plants
if check.last
-> speaks
endif
-> END

~ speaks
set hag_garden_spoke
Narrator: The poppies nod, the mandrake leaves curl, and the whole bed answers at once in a sweet, sticky whisper, like a child who knows a secret.
Narrator: "The round one picked a basket of us at dawn for the baking, and said sorry to each one. She always says sorry."
Narrator: "The pretty one flew home over us at midnight on a broom, so low she brushed the poppies, and went in at the loft window. She hides it in the rafters, where her mother never looks up."
reveal rafters_broom
-> END
